  "id": "romanian-deadlift",
  "name": "Romanian and Stiff-Leg Deadlift",
  "definition": "A bilateral unsupported barbell hip hinge with planted feet and a braced spine. The ordinary Romanian Deadlift starts at the top, holds slight knee flexion, and reverses near mid-shin without touching the floor; the distinct Stiff-Leg Deadlift keeps the knees extended and follows its reviewed floor-contact protocol. Hip extension is the sole dynamic prime. The straight-spine instruction supports resisting spinal flexion rather than inventing dynamic spinal extension. Deficit, floor-touch Romanian, dumbbell, kettlebell, staggered, and single-leg variants remain outside the active roster. Ulnar and radial wrist extensors and flexors, and finger extensors, receive categorical grip-control stabilizer credit based on related studies, not direct measurement of these exact phases or universal training stimulus.",
